<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank reserves fell in latest week.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank reserves fell in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves fell by $128 million to $17.242 billion in the week ended October 25.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>		   October 25    October 18   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve   17.242	  17.370	 12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve     1.383	   1.383	  1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve   18.625	  18.753	 13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $112 million to $28.042 billion in the week ending October 11, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
